  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), the page state: MPStorage thread: its first-post page (rendered) and the edit form of that first post with the real JSON in `content_form` (several namespaces, exact bytes; redact pseudos/hashes consistently); ideally a second one near the 64 KiB cap or with a non-BMP character; then the LOT-004 (#41) exporter `mpstorage-page` kind on the page\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: MPStorage thread: its first-post page (rendered) and the edit form of that first post with the real JSON in `content_form` (several namespaces, exact bytes; redact pseudos/hashes consistently); ideally a second one near the 64 KiB cap or with a non-BMP character; then the LOT-004 (#41) exporter `mpstorage-page` kind on the page\n\nNote: the thread is in `R13u1` but was never opened (HFR-PROTOCOL MPStorage read row, LOT-004 (#41) spec); without it LOT-038 (#65) cannot start (LESSONS 35-36)\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it (LOT-002 (#39)..005 tooling); one PR per batch of captures; the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-038 (#65), LOT-052 (#78)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\n`docs/LOTS.md` \"Capture backlog (Mac)\", copied from the frozen old issue [francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#98](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/98).\n",
